\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {III}{\ignorespaces Depolarizing robustness for the restricted projector-cone prepare-and-measure fragments used in this paper. The listed rays are used both as rank-one preparations and as rank-one effects. The noise is the state-side depolarizing map $\rho \DOTSB \mapstochar \rightarrow \operatorname  {tr}(\rho )\mathbf  {1}_d/d$. The reported values are numerical optima with residuals chopped to zero, except for the Yu--Oh 13-ray value, for which an exact diagonal certificate was separately audited. Rational reconstructions of the other decimals are intentionally not displayed in the main table.}}{13}{table.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:results}{{III}{13}{Depolarizing robustness for the restricted projector-cone prepare-and-measure fragments used in this paper. The listed rays are used both as rank-one preparations and as rank-one effects. The noise is the state-side depolarizing map $\rho \mapsto \tr (\rho )\id _d/d$. The reported values are numerical optima with residuals chopped to zero, except for the Yu--Oh 13-ray value, for which an exact diagonal certificate was separately audited. Rational reconstructions of the other decimals are intentionally not displayed in the main table}{table.3}{}}
